# agent-sandbox environment

## Running commands
{{if .Hook}}- Run shell commands with your normal Bash/Monitor tools; a PreToolUse hook transparently routes each one through the sandbox.
- Command output is returned inline in the tool result.
{{else}}- The Bash and Monitor tools are disabled; use the `run_command` MCP tool to run shell commands.
- Command output is written to files; read the returned stdout/stderr paths.
{{end}}- Allowed commands run on the host; all others run in an isolated container.

## Filesystem: host and container share the same paths
The project directory is bind-mounted into the container at the same absolute path it has on the host (an identity mount), so a project path means the same file everywhere:
- Host commands (the allow list below) run in the real project directory using real host absolute paths.
- Container commands run inside the sandbox with the project mounted at that same path (the working directory); HOME is `/tmp`.
- A project absolute path you see from a container command is equally valid for host-side file tools and host commands — no translation needed. Only paths outside the project (e.g. under HOME) differ between host and container.
{{if .Safe}}
## Safe command wrappers
Prefer these validated wrappers over running the tool directly; each refuses known-dangerous invocations before running:
{{range .Safe}}- `agent-sandbox safe {{.Use}}` — {{.Short}}
{{end}}{{end}}
